{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutesProtonMass","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutesProtonMass","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Inverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.five_averaged_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.five_averaged_crossings","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L196-L207","doc":"For 5 interface crossings (deuteron):\n(σ−h/2)⁵ = (1+h²/4)² × (σ−h/2).\nThe 5 averaged crossings reduce to ONE effective crossing\ntimes the scalar (1+h²/4)² ≈ 1.022. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.scalar_eq_two_q_squared_over_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.scalar_eq_two_q_squared_over_4","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L190-L194","doc":"The scalar value (1+h²/4) equals [2]_q²/4 = (q+q⁻¹)²/4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.averaged_crossing_squared_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.averaged_crossing_squared_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L168-L188","doc":"The averaged crossing operator σ_avg = σ − h/2 satisfies\nσ_avg² = 1 + h²/4 = [2]_q²/4 (SCALAR — identity matrix).\n\nProof: from the Hecke relation σ² = hσ + 1:\n  (σ − h/2)² = σ² − hσ + h²/4 = (hσ+1) − hσ + h²/4 = 1 + h²/4.  QED\n\nConsequence: even powers of the averaged crossing are SCALAR\n(no operator content). Odd powers are linear in σ. For n\ninterface crossings:\n  n even: (σ−h/2)ⁿ = (1+h²/4)^{n/2} · I  (pure scalar)\n  n odd:  (σ−h/2)ⁿ = (1+h²/4)^{(n−1)/2} · (σ−h/2)  (linear)\n\nThis means the interface's quadratic terms factor out as a\nuniversal scalar, and only ONE effective crossing carries the\noperator-valued binding information. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.mpOverMe_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.mpOverMe_factored","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L127-L132","doc":"The proton mass-ratio decomposition factors as\n(Vol(B₃)/ℏ²) · lw_A · spectralCorr.  PROVED (definitional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.borromeanChar_laurent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.borromeanChar_laurent","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L113-L125","doc":"The Borromean (2,1) character in Laurent form.  This matches the\nHoefsmit-derived trace tr_{(2,1)}[(σ₁⁻¹σ₂)³] = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶\n(verified symbolically from the explicit Hoefsmit σ₁ = diag(q,−q⁻¹),\nσ₂ solved from Hecke + braid): χ = −q⁶ + 3q⁴ − 3q² + 4 − 3q⁻² +\n3q⁻⁴ − q⁻⁶.  So the spectral correction's input character is\nderived, not asserted.  PROVED. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.borromean_char_arccos_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.borromean_char_arccos_arg","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L104-L111","doc":"The spectral arccos argument is exactly χ/2, where χ is the\nBorromean character on V_{(2,1)} (χ = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶). Hence\nspectralCorr's argument equals 1 − 3h⁴/2 − h⁶/2. PROVED. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.h_eq_qp1_hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.h_eq_qp1_hbar","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L97-L102","doc":"KEY IDENTITY: h = (q+1)·ℏ.\nThis connects the two routes through the substrate structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.lwProduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.lwProduction","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L68-L71","doc":"Route 1 effective linking weight:\nlw_eff = m_p(Route 1) / (Vol(B₃)/ℏ²).\nThis is what the substrate identity IMPLICITLY uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.mpOverMe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.mpOverMe","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L61-L66","doc":"Route 2 decomposition of the proton mass ratio:\nm_p/m_e = (Vol(B₃)/ℏ²) · lw_A · spectralCorr = geomScale · lwSpectral.\nNumerically (q₀, 50 dps): the leading (Vol/ℏ²)·lw_A reproduces the\n+2.89% VolDensity gap; the derived spectralCorr factor (≈0.97112)\ncloses it to ~130 ppm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.geomScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.geomScale","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L58-L59","doc":"Geometric scale Vol(B₃)/ℏ² = 8G/ℏ² (G = Catalan, archimedean). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.lwSpectral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.lwSpectral","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L55-L56","doc":"Route 2 linking weight: lw_A × spectral correction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.lwA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.lwA","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The Family-A linking weight lw_A = 5/2 + 3h²/4 (PROVED, Family A). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.spectralCorr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.spectralCorr","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L46-L50","doc":"Route 2: the spectral correction factor θ/(8ℏ²), where the\nspectral angle θ = arccos(χ/2) and χ = borromeanChar is the\nexact Borromean character on V_{(2,1)}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.borromeanChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.borromeanChar","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L41-L44","doc":"The EXACT Hoefsmit Borromean character on the standard irrep\nV_{(2,1)}: χ^{(2,1)}(B₃) = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.F_Bor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.F_Bor","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Route 1: F_Bor = |tr_M(B₃)| × [3]_q!/q³.\nThe substrate identity gives m_p/m_e = 2(m_μ/m_e)F_Bor − 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L34-L35","doc":"The substrate Planck constant ℏ = (q−1)/q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRoutes.h","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean#L31-L32","doc":"The deformation parameter h = q − q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0}]}